cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Peptacular: A Python package for amino acid sequence analysis with ProForma 2.1"
abstract: >-
  Peptacular is a typed Python package for representing and analyzing peptide
  and protein sequences written in ProForma 2.1 notation. It parses ProForma
  strings into structured ProFormaAnnotation objects that can be inspected,
  modified, and serialized. The representation covers sequence annotations,
  chemical modifications, terminal annotations, charge states, isotope labels,
  and other constructs defined by the supported ProForma compliance level.
  Analysis functions calculate neutral mass, mass-to-charge ratio, elemental
  composition, isotope distributions, fragment ions, digestion products, and
  physicochemical sequence properties. Users can work through annotation
  objects or a functional API. Functional calls accept individual sequences or
  collections, with parallel processing available for batch calculations. The
  package uses tacular for shared amino-acid, element, modification, protease,
  and ion reference data. Peptacular is intended for proteomics software,
  analysis pipelines, and research scripts that need one consistent sequence
  notation across parsing, annotation, calculation, and serialization. It
  requires Python 3.12 or later.
